@page "/components/table-of-contents"

<PageTitle>TableOfContents — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">TableOfContents</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> built from entries the page supplies — it knows the links, not the
    document, so the headings and the ids stay written down once instead of twice.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="TableOfContentsExample.razor"><TableOfContentsExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A short page needs no index. And if the section ids are generated rather than written by hand,
    the links rot silently — a table of contents that points nowhere is worse than none, so keep
    the ids next to the headings.
</p>
